  "question_type": "MCQ",
  "question": "If B is a non-singular matrix and A is a square matrix, then $|B^{-1}AB|$ is equal to:",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "Using determinant properties:<br /><br />$|B^{-1}AB| = |B^{-1}| \\cdot |A| \\cdot |B|$<br /><br />But $|B^{-1}| = \\frac{1}{|B|}$<br /><br />So: $|B^{-1}AB| = \\frac{1}{|B|} \\cdot |A| \\cdot |B| = |A|$<br /><br />Therefore, $|B^{-1}AB| = |A|$",
